PDFXI
=====

PDFXI is an independent clean-room implementation. It is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or sponsored by Adobe Inc. "Adobe", "Acrobat", and related marks
are trademarks of Adobe Inc. No Adobe source code, binaries, icons, help text,
or other proprietary assets are included.

Third-party components and their licenses are listed in `deny.toml` and in the
generated `docs/THIRD_PARTY.md`. Notable runtime dependencies are expected to
include:

- PDFium (BSD-3-Clause) for rendering and text extraction.
- lopdf (MIT) for PDF object manipulation.
- egui/eframe (MIT OR Apache-2.0) for the desktop UI.
- Tesseract (Apache-2.0) as an optional OCR sidecar.

Optional external converters (LibreOffice, a headless browser, Ghostscript) are
not bundled by default and remain the user's responsibility.

